          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP479 Memorial Park Calgary [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It seemed like a good idea to drop in here before my work day, so that’s what I did. Easy find of a nice geodetic marker in a great setting. TFTBC.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="749212150">
          <groundspeak:date>2018-02-25T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="5323897">brendan714</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP479 Memorial Park Calgary

N 51° 02.468 W 114° 04.176&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for some winter downtown caching with Hunthikers.  I noticed the brass cap not too far from our parking point, and we followed some snowy trails over to GZ.  Thank goodness Hunthikers had found this one previously - he swiped away some snow and the cap was found!  I probably wouldn't have found it otherwise.  That said, it would be such an easy find with no snow!  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I've visited Central Memorial Park dozens of times before - I can't believe I haven't (FOUND) this cap until now.  One of my favourite downtown parks.  Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="704448773">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-07-23T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1685537">nosweat6060</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP479 Memorial Park Calgary [FOUND]

I am making good brass cap use of a few days in Calgary. This morning (Sunday) I set out a plan for 6 caps in the urban area of Calgary. Sunday morning is an ideal time for a visitor to tour the downtown. The plan was for 6 caps - with a couple involving some walking as well. I have some super photos of the city as well. Thanks again to ofth &amp; vdD for setting up and maintaining this activity. I am glad you did! This was cap #2 for today.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
